    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Throttled [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x17302; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 4 duration target of the VVEL selector: the throttled mode and the late cold path. Interpolated by engine speed and scaled by 0.05. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x17302 bound to accessor 0x5f468 through literal 0x5f780, accessor 0x70514 through literal 0x71030, accessor 0x70514 through literal 0x712b8. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/analysis/valve-timing/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/analysis/valve-timing/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. The 0.05 multiplication, offset arithmetic and shared dispatcher word domain do not establish physical duration degrees. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_0005F468 at callsite 0x5F616 through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x2893C and by FUN_00070514 at three callsites; the 0.05 factor is the float literal 0x3D4CCCCC at 0x5F784. Stock bytes are identical to JK78C 0x00016D14. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
