  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xFDC5" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Shaft Angle Monitor Floor - A, Second Copy [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x1B8DE; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Second copy of monitor floor A: FUN_00062774 interpolates it by the word 0xFFFE81C8 into 0xFFFEAA76, one of the four floor words 0xFFFEA422, 0xFFFEA424, 0xFFFEAA76, and 0xFFFEAA78 whose maximum the deficit monitors FUN_000DFFE6 compare with the measured control-shaft angle. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x1b8de bound to accessor 0x62774 through literal 0x627a4. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x/512 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x*512. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/analysis/valve-timing/JK78C.vvel.md:491-499, defs/analysis/valve-timing/JK78C.vvel.md:525-530, vvel_shaft_angle_axis/axis, vvel_command_shaft_angle/tbl. A shared integer domain, maximum, subtraction, absolute-value correction or word bound preserves count arithmetic. None independently fixes 512 counts per physical degree. An RPM or CVTC input grid cannot establish the returned shaft-coordinate unit. The upstream coordinate scale itself has no physical grounding in the finite sources. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by FUN_00062774 at callsite 0x62780 through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x28910. No direct call reaches the reader; its entry address is the word at 0x221D8 of a function-pointer list. The maximum with the primary floor words fixes the 1/512 degree domain. Stock bytes are identical to the primary table 0x00016698. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
