  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xFBB0" flags="0x0">
    <title>Fuel Compensation - Coefficient Curve [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x13F1A; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Fuel-compensation curve selected by state code 8, derived from VVEL input mode 15. The selected channel replaces the default surface at full current-state weight. The physical unit, engineering conversion and neutral value are unestablished. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x13f1a bound to accessor 0x30810 through literal 0x3116c, accessor 0x44f1c through literal 0x45500. Coordinator 0x00044f1c selects this curve instead of the default fuel-compensation surface for state code 8 (VVEL input mode 15). At full current-state weight, changes to the default surface are replaced by this channel. During a transition, the coordinator mixes current_channel*w with previous_channel*(0x8000-w), using the held previous output during an interrupted transition, then normalizes by 0x8000 and clamps the result to 0..255. The weight 0x8000 is 1.0. Stock driving reachability of input modes 5 and 15 is unconfirmed on every image. The physical unit, engineering conversion and neutral value are unestablished; raw 128 is not qualified as neutral. No engine-bank identity is established. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
