  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xE4C" flags="0x0">
    <title>End of Injection Angle - Base</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x16540; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Base end-of-injection angle over an explicit eight-point engine-speed axis. The injection writer interpolates the eight uint16 cells, adds one or two correction bytes, and stores 2*min(sum, 209) to the end-of-injection word, the delay in 2 crank degrees per count from the reference tooth of the scheduled channel to the end of the pulse. A cell of x counts ends the pulse 4*x - 590 degrees after the following intake TDC, as a cell of JK08A 00012302 does. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x16540 bound to accessor 0x7f4e0 through literal 0x7fa04. Writer 0007f4e0 loads the curve from literal 0007fa04 for the calls at 0007f91a and 0007f95c to wrapper 00028910 on axis 00016550 and engine-speed word fffe81b6. It adds byte fffea7ee, and on the second call also byte fffea2ad, before the clamp, and stores the result to fffe89a2.</description>
