  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xB2EA" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Characteristic [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x16090; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Monotonic duration characteristic of the VVEL duration correction FUN_0005751E: looked up by its first duration argument x512, clamped to 0..100.0, over the axis 0x00017612 and scaled by 2^-18. FUN_0005751E subtracts from the result a 16x16 lookup of 0x0000CDC8 over the axes 0x000158D2 and 0x00017632, indexed by the margin of its second over its third argument and by the same duration index. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x16090 bound to accessor 0x5751e through literal 0x576f0. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*2^-18; proposed editor-grid inverse x*2^18. Origin: on JK78C 0x00015AA2, the float literal 2^-18 at 0x56090. Recorded code interpretation: Read by FUN_0005751E through the literal-pool word 0x000576F0, loaded at 0x0005758C. FUN_0005751E differs from JK78C FUN_00055E78: it clamps the lookup duration to 0..100.0, keeps the 2^-18 scale, and subtracts the correction surface 0x0000CDC8; JK78C FUN_00055E78 instead passes the scaled value to the ratio corrections FUN_00055F2C and FUN_00055FF2. Besides FUN_0005751E, the code graph records only 0x0005B998 as a reader of the axis 0x00017612, so no inverse lookup over this curve is bound on the layout. Stock bytes are identical to JK78C 0x00015AA2. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
