    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x173C2; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 15 intake-cam target of the VVEL selector, interpolated by engine speed. Zero at raw 0x8000, 0.5 per count. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x173c2 bound to accessor 0x5f468 through literal 0x5f770. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: (x-32768)*0.5 degCA; proposed editor-grid inverse x*2+32768. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/analysis/valve-timing/JK78C.vvel.md:409-428, defs/analysis/valve-timing/JK78C.vvel.md:495-505, intake_cvtc_target_running_axis/axis. The resolver arithmetic establishes a centered numeric output only where the recorded conversion path is given. It does not establish physical camshaft/crankshaft degrees. Uniform zero counts cannot prove a slope. A proved RPM or temperature coordinate does not prove the table output unit. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_0005F468 at callsite 0x5F5F6 through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x2893C and converted with the float literals 0xC6800000 and 0x3F000000. The stock curve peaks at 35.0 where the JK78C curve 0x00016DC4 peaks at 30.0. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
