    <title>Target Mixture Multiplier - High-Detonation State</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x13F0A; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. High-detonation target multiplier: Q7 factor applied to the deviation of the 0000a9aa target mixture from 128 when ffff2466 bit 6 selects the high-detonation surface, sat_u8(128 + ((m - 128) * t &gt;&gt; 7)). Stock 128..154 on engine-speed axis 00011cd8 (ffff11ae) scales the enrichment from 1 at 4000 rpm to 1.203 at 4800 rpm and above. Public HR A2L name Target AFR Table (High Detonation). The physical purpose follows the consumer chain 0005594a -&gt; ffff15eb -&gt; ffff22e8. Definition address projected from JK08A 00012552 through JK08A-1ND.definition-addresses.csv: Stage 0007e3ae enables this eight-byte curve under fffe9488.bit6, indexes it by byte fffe81a8 over explicit axis 000137c1 and applies it as a Q7 multiplier of the main surface's deviation from 128 before byte saturation. Its factor normalization is code; the RPM-byte conversion remains a candidate. Static diagnostic context: ENG SPEED [code, homologous_vq35hr, via axis evidence: indexed_by].</description>
