    <title>Knock Threshold by Evaluator Channel</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x122C8; 6 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence candidate. Knock Slice Map: per-evaluator-channel knock threshold by engine speed. A calculated metric exceeding the interpolated threshold contributes to increasing the knock count. On 7mfk, 00049ffc selects one of six one-based evaluator rows, interpolates 16 uint16 cells along axis 00015340, and writes the selected word at ffff2144 + 2*(c-1). Its bounded domain is 1 &lt;= c &lt;= 6; the accessor has no channel guard. JK08A stock rows 3 and 5 contain raw threshold 65535 at every cell. The selected raw word enters comparison in 0004a238; metric production, comparison outcome and count publication are outside the bounded lookup proof. Both neighboring cells are loaded, including 0001114e on the last row endpoint. The catalog identifies rows as cylinders, but exact lookup code does not establish physical cylinder or sensor order. The engineering threshold scale remains candidate. Definition address projected from JK08A 0001108e through JK08A-1ND.definition-addresses.csv: Exact 1ND0A and 1ND3B images load table 000122c8 through MOV.L at 0006e87e and pool 0006ea98. Accessor 0006e854 selects row table + 32*(c-1), supplies unsigned word axis 00016bc2 and coordinate fffe81ee to 0002893c, and stores the raw word at fffe9138 + 2*(c-1). Its sole interpolation call is ordinal 0 of 1. Caller 0006ea18 compares the selected uint32 metric against 0x80000000 + uint16(threshold) using strict CMP/HI at 0006ed64. These operands and the consumer support raw threshold-role homology with 7mfk:0001108e. Target axis knots end at 464,504,544, unlike the 7mfk knots 448,480,512. Target execution, full arithmetic and ABI equivalence, engineering scale and physical channel identity remain unestablished.</description>
