    <title>Gear Transition Request - Recovery Decrement [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x15EB0; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Eight-word recovery array indexed by min(latched target-gear index uint8[ffff1077],7), as described in defs/analysis/valve-timing/JK78C.vvel.md, section "Data flow". When the selected recovery byte is zero, subtract the unsigned entry from signed state ffff36b0 with a -32768 floor, then publish the maximum of that state and the independently bounded current candidate at ffff36ae. The inactive-transition path forces the recovery byte to zero; the active path uses the target-gear index ffff1077, which can also be zero. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x15eb0 bound to accessor 0xabc6e through literal 0xac290. Stock 1ND3B leaves the conditioner unexecuted: dispatcher 000ab184 calls it only while bit 0 of ROM8[0000839f] and bit 7 of the mode flags ROM8[00008a2e] are clear, and the flags hold 0x80. The frame 0x174 receive record at 00009714 is inactive. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
