  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xB906" flags="0x0">
    <title>Engine Speed Limit - Throttle Request - Oil Temperature</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x17222; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Eight-word oil-temperature threshold of the rotational-speed request limiter, read through 000282f4 on the explicit word axis 00016a64, which it shares with rev_limit_fuel_cut_curves/tbl. Its coordinate is rev_fuel_cut_selector/ram at ffff10e5, the filtered raw oil-thermistor code. While ffff4573.bit4 is set, the word published at ffff1a3c can lower the calibrated threshold, and it also bounds the downward threshold ramp. Producer 000bdf90 sets that bit by a hysteretic comparison of the code with ROM8[00008aef] and ROM8[00008af0] and leaves it clear while the oil-sensor fault records are set. This curve has no scalar-to-curve binding to the canonical alternate threshold. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x17222 bound to accessor 0xa8f02 through literal 0xa91dc. Stock 1ND0A and 1ND3B apply the curve: bit 0 of ROM8[00008561] enables the oil sensor, producer 000df018 compares selector fffe80ed with ROM8[00008bd1] = 20 and hysteresis ROM8[00008bd2] = 1 and copies the result to fffeb89d.bit2 while the oil-sensor fault records are clear, and the reader tests that bit at 000a904c. On the stock oil-thermistor curve 0001456a, codes 15 to 20 read about 151 to 136 C [cand], as on JK78C.</description>
