  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x9077" flags="0x0">
    <title>Timing Float Ratio Response Surface [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x11E48; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Response surface of the ratio-response builder over the exponent axis timing_float_ratio_response_axis_x and the ratio axis timing_float_ratio_response_axis_y. The stored surface is x-major: each row of 16 words belongs to one x breakpoint, the exponent times 131072, and each column to one y breakpoint, the ratio times 32768, so the editor X axis is the ratio axis. Every stock cell on every layout equals 32768 * (y / 32768)^(x / 131072) within 1.03 counts, so cell / 32768 = (y / 32768)^(x / 131072). The builder indexes it after the separately computed (v-1)/v transformation, and its output contributes to the float producer tree. The issue #114 float model also reads it with both axes, through charge_ratio_temperature_lookup on JK78C. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x11e48 bound to accessor 0x61120 through literal 0x614d4. Stock lookup status: active. Scheduler entry 00022194 calls the float model root 00060756; reader 00061120 reads this role without a calibration branch. The root publishes the words fffea43c, fffea43e, fffea566 and fffea752 to the consumer 00061b28, whose output byte fffe9400 nonlinear_transition_controller and four other functions read. The issue #114 float model also reads it at 00055aec. Stored counts are retained. The physical quantities of the inputs of reader 00061120 are unresolved. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
