    <title>Timing Float Low Branch Response Curve [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x17162; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Alternative response curve of the branch-response builder. The reader selects between this curve and the shared absolute-response curve according to its transformed float input, then scales the selected unsigned word. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0x17162 bound to accessor 0x61ea6 through literal 0x620d4. Stock lookup status: active. Scheduler entry 0002219c runs 000736f4, which calls the float consumer 00061b28 unconditionally at 00073806; reader 00061ea6 reads this role without a calibration branch. The consumer publishes byte fffe9400, which nonlinear_transition_controller and four other functions read. Stored counts are retained. Physical quantities and engineering conversions are unresolved. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
