    <title>Map 4 - Ignition Timing Surface - VVEL State Codes 6 and 7 [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x135500; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Ignition surface for state codes 6 and 7, VVEL modes 13 and 14, of the mode-selected half of the ignition coordinator FUN_00074D98, the half that stock ROM8[0x8A2B] = 0xBA (bit 5 set) executes. Stock ROM8[0x8A2C] = 0x1C (bit 3 set) selects the surface by the state-code byte 0xFFFEB6DE, which the mapper FUN_0004C4B8 derives from the VVEL mode: mode 5 gives code 2, mode 3 code 3, mode 10 code 4, mode 12 code 5, mode 13 code 6, mode 14 code 7, mode 15 code 8, and every other mode code 1. The coordinator takes the low seven bits of the lookup and crossfades the previous and current state values by the progress word 0xFFFEB6DC, where 0x8000 is 1.0. Common-definition Map 4 storage is projected from 0xA6D0. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. This view edits mask 0x7F and preserves the other bits in each cell. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0xa6d0 bound to accessor 0x74d98 through literal 0x74fac. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x-64 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x+64. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/registries/JK08A.findings.csv:41, ignition_gated_surface_1/tbl. The canonical PID0E closure is not the executed target-native path. Equal surface bytes and a common field/coordinator role do not reproduce that complete target arithmetic and diagnostic publication. x-64 applies to the low-seven field only; applying it to the full byte would include the independent flag. This is an adjustment hypothesis, not absolute spark angle. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Byte-identical to the 1ME3B surface 0xA604. The 8x8 lookup 0x000285B4 serves the four state-code surfaces of this coordinator. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
